🔗 OLTP vs OLAP
Feature	OLTP (Database)	OLAP (Data Warehouse)
Purpose	Transactions	Analytics & Reporting
Schema	Normalized	Dimensional (Fact/Dim)
Example	MySQL, Postgres	Snowflake, BigQuery
Query type	Simple inserts/updates	Complex joins, aggregations
OLTP: Online Transaction Processing → fast, concurrent, normalized tables for day-to-day operations.

OLAP: Online Analytical Processing → historical, aggregated, dimensional modeling for BI and ML.

ETL/ELT pipelines: Connect OLTP → OLAP.

🏗️ Data Engineering Pipeline
OLTP Database (MySQL/Postgres): Raw transactional data (customers, orders, payments).

ETL/ELT Process: Extract, Transform, Load using tools like Airflow, dbt, Spark.

OLAP Data Warehouse (Snowflake/BigQuery): Stores fact and dimension tables.

Analytics Layer: Dashboards, BI, ML features built on top of fact/dim schema.

